[55.282, "o", "     \"advice\": \"For your glucose, keep meals regular and use the plate pattern at lunch and dinner: 1/2 vegetables, 1/4 wholegrains or staples, and 1/4 protein. Choose brown rice, oats or wholemeal bread, paired with fish, chicken, tofu, eggs, beans or lean meat. Breakfast ideas: oats with plain yoghurt and fruit, or wholemeal toast with egg and tomatoes. Hawker options include economy rice with brown rice, two vegetables and one protein, or soup-based yong tau foo with vegetables, tofu, egg or fish; ask for less gravy or sauce. Choose water, kopi kosong or teh siew dai; snacks can be fruit, plain yoghurt or unsalted nuts. Avoid crash diets.\\n\\nFor an indoor morning activity near Woodlands, join Morning Chair Strength & Balance at Woodlands Community Club on Tuesday at 8:30am (45 minutes, light intensity; ACT001). Start gently and stop if you feel dizzy, have chest discomfort or unusual breathlessness. As your screening risk is High, please follow up with a clinic too.\",\r\n"]
[55.282, "o", "     \"confidence\": \"high\",\r\n"]
